From 05e187495a2a3578f9f48ebae16a0cc7f5a616bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 21 Jun 2026 18:24:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03325/11362] [outer-loop] arc: promote epochs=30 warm-start
 prior (transfer 0.314 -> 0.5485), validates leak fix at scale

The epochs=30 GPU pretrain -- the run that previously OOM-leaked the box to 101GB host RAM --
now completes cleanly at 1.8GB RSS (exit 0), confirming the corpus-load .npz re-decompression
fix holds at the 12.7k-transition scale. The longer pretrain transfers materially better:
mean changed-cell recall warm 0.314 (e10/fs60) -> 0.5485 (e30/fs80), 5/5 held-out games
(tn36 0.875, sc25 0.732, ka59 0.484). Promoted to models/arc_dynamics_prior.pt; the validated
e10 prior is preserved in git history + /tmp. This is the warm-start the live TTT agent loads.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
